aba-convert.c is copied verbatim from payslate's legacy/aba-convert as it stood on
the day of this spike: the converter reads the whole input once and writes only
after the control trailer reconciles. It is one file; the parse-and-reconcile loop
lives inside main.

reader.h / reader.c are this spike's own work: the same parse-and-reconcile logic
factored into a buffer function (read_batch) that takes bytes instead of a file, so
KLEE can call it directly. Splitting the reader out this way is what let KLEE run on
it, and the same split is worth making in payslate's converter.
